t3\t\tする\nR\tこれる\$\t\t\tv1\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\tくる\nR\t来れる\$\t\t\tv1\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\t来る\nR\t來れる\$\t\t\tv1\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\t來る\nT\tpotential or passive\tpotential or passive\t1. Indicates an action received from an action performer. 2. Expresses respect for the subject of action performer. 3. Indicates a state of being (naturally) capable of doing an action. Usage: Attach られる to the irrealis form (未然形) of ichidan verbs. する becomes せられる, くる becomes こられる\nR\tられる\$\t\t\tv1\tv1\ts\t0\t3\t\tる\nR\tざれる\$\t\t\tv1\tvz\ts\t0\t3\t\tずる\nR\tぜられる\$\t\t\tv1\tvz\ts\t0\t4\t\tずる\nR\tせられる\$\t\t\tv1\tvs\ts\t0\t4\t\tする\nR\t為られる\$\t\t\tv1\tvs\ts\t0\t4\t\t為る\nR\tこられる\$\t\t\tv1\tvk\ts\t0\t4\t\tくる\nR\t来られる\$\t\t\tv1\tvk\ts\t0\t4\t\t来る\nR\t來られる\$\t\t\tv1\tvk\ts\t0\t4\t\t來る\nT\tvolitional\tvolitional\t1. Expresses speaker's will or intention. 2. Expresses an invitation to the other party. 3. (Used in …ようとする) Indicates being on the verge of initiating an action or transforming a state. 4. Indicates an inference of a matter. Usage: Attach よう to the irrealis form (未然形) of ichidan verbs. Attach う to the irrealis form (未然形) of godan verbs after -o euphonic change form. Attach かろう to the stem of i-adjectives (4th meaning only).\nR\tよう\$\t\t\t\tv1\ts\t0\t2\t\tる\nR\tやう\$\t\t\t\tv1\ts\t0\t2\t\tる\nR\tおう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tう\nR\tはう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tう\nR\tこう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tく\nR\tかう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tく\nR\tごう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tぐ\nR\tがう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tぐ\nR\tそう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tす\nR\tさう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tす\nR\tとう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tつ\nR\tたう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tつ\nR\tのう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tぬ\nR\tなう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tぬ\nR\tぼう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tぶ\nR\tばう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tぶ\nR\tもう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tむ\nR\tまう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tむ\nR\tろう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tる\nR\tらう\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t2\t\tる\nR\tじよう\$\t\t\t\tvz\ts\t0\t3\t\tずる\nR\tじやう\$\t\t\t\tvz\ts\t0\t3\t\tずる\nR\tしよう\$\t\t\t\tvs\ts\t0\t3\t\tする\nR\tしやう\$\t\t\t\tvs\ts\t0\t3\t\tする\nR\t為よう\$\t\t\t\tvs\ts\t0\t3\t\t為る\nR\t為やう\$\t\t\t\tvs\ts\t0\t3\t\t為る\n",
    "R\tこよう\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\tくる\nR\tこやう\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\tくる\nR\t来よう\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\t来る\nR\t来やう\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\t来る\nR\t來よう\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\t來る\nR\t來やう\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\t來る\nR\tましょう\$\t\t\t\t-ます\ts\t0\t4\t\tます\nR\tませう\$\t\t\t\t-ます\ts\t0\t3\t\tます\nR\tかろう\$\t\t\t\tadj-i\ts\t0\t3\t\tい\nR\tからう\$\t\t\t\tadj-i\ts\t0\t3\t\tい\nT\tvolitional slang\tvolitional slang\tContraction of volitional form + か 1. Expresses speaker's will or intention. 2. Expresses an invitation to the other party. Usage: Replace final う with っ of volitional form then add か. For example: 行こうか -> 行こっか.\nR\tよっか\$\t\t\t\tv1\ts\t0\t3\t\tる\nR\tおっか\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t3\t\tう\nR\tこっか\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t3\t\tく\nR\tごっか\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t3\t\tぐ\nR\tそっか\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t3\t\tす\nR\tとっか\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t3\t\tつ\nR\tのっか\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t3\t\tぬ\nR\tぼっか\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t3\t\tぶ\nR\tもっか\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t3\t\tむ\nR\tろっか\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t3\t\tる\nR\tじよっか\$\t\t\t\tvz\ts\t0\t4\t\tずる\nR\tしよっか\$\t\t\t\tvs\ts\t0\t4\t\tする\nR\t為よっか\$\t\t\t\tvs\ts\t0\t4\t\t為る\nR\tこよっか\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t4\t\tくる\nR\t来よっか\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t4\t\t来る\nR\t來よっか\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t4\t\t來る\nR\tましょっか\$\t\t\t\t-ます\ts\t0\t5\t\tます\nT\t-まい\t-まい\tNegative volitional form of verbs. 1. Expresses speaker's assumption that something is likely not true. 2. Expresses speaker's will or intention not to do something. Usage: Attach まい to the dictionary form (終止形) of verbs. Attach まい to the irrealis form (未然形) of ichidan verbs. する becomes しまい, くる becomes こまい\nR\tまい\$\t\t\t\tv\ts\t0\t2\t\t\nR\tまい\$\t\t\t\tv1\ts\t0\t2\t\tる\nR\tじまい\$\t\t\t\tvz\ts\t0\t3\t\tずる\nR\tしまい\$\t\t\t\tvs\ts\t0\t3\t\tする\nR\t為まい\$\t\t\t\tvs\ts\t0\t3\t\t為る\nR\tこまい\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\tくる\nR\t来まい\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\t来る\nR\t來まい\$\t\t\t\tvk\ts\t0\t3\t\t來る\nR\tまい\$\t\t\t\t-ます\ts\t0\t2\t\t\nT\t-おく\t-おく\tTo do certain things in advance in preparation (or in anticipation) of latter needs. Usage: Attach おく to the て-form of verbs. Attach でおく after ない negative form of verbs. Contracts to とく・どく in speech.\nR\tておく\$\t\t\tv5\t-て\ts\t0\t3\t\tて\nR\tでおく\$\t\t\tv5\t-て\ts\t0\t3\t\tで\nR\tとく\$\t\t\tv5\t-て\ts\t0\t2\t\tて\nR\tどく\$\t\t\tv5\t-て\ts\t0\t2\t\tで\nR\tないでおく\$\t\t\tv5\tadj-i\ts\t0\t5\t\tない\nR\tないどく\$\t\t\tv5\tadj-i\ts\t0\t4\t\tない\nT\t-いる\t-いる\t1. Indicates an action continues or progresses to a point in time. 2. Indicates an action is completed and remains as is. 3. Indicates a state or condition that can be taken to be the result of undergoing some change. Usage: Attach いる to the て-form of verbs. い can be dropped in speech. Attach でいる after ない negative form of verbs. (Slang) Attach おる to the て-form of verbs. Contracts to とる・でる in speech.\nR\tている\$\t\t\tv1\t-て\ts\t0\t3\t\tて\nR\tてゐる\$\t\t\tv1\t-て\ts\t0\t3\t\tて\nR\tておる\$\t\t\tv5\t-て\ts\t0\t3\t\tて\nR\tてる\$\t\t\tv1p\t-て\ts\t0\t2\t\tて\nR\tでいる\$\t\t\tv1\t-て\ts\t0\t3\t\tで\nR\tでゐる\$\t\t\tv1\t-て\ts\t0\t3\t\tで\nR\tでおる\$\t\t\tv5\t-て\ts\t0\t3\t\tで\nR\tでる\$\t\t\tv1p\t-て\ts\t0\t2\t\tで\nR\tとる\$\t\t\tv5\t-て\ts\t0\t2\t\tて\nR\tないでいる\$\t\t\tv1\tadj-i\ts\t0\t5\t\tない\nR\tないでゐる\$\t\t\tv1\tadj-i\ts\t0\t5\t\tない\nT\t-ふ\t-ふ\tHistorical kana orthography (歴史的仮名遣い) for the dictionary/terminal form of ワ行五段 verbs, used in pre-1946 and literary/classical Japanese (e.g. 思ふ for 思う).\nR\tふ\$\t\t\t\tv5\ts\t0\t1\t\tう\nT\t-き\t-き\tAttributive form (連体形) of i-adjectives. An archaic form that remains in modern Japanese.\nR\tき\$\t\t\t\tadj-i\ts\t0\t1\t\tい\nT\t-げ\t-げ\tDescribes a person's appearance. Shows feelings of the person. Usage: Attach げ or 気 to the stem of i-adjectives\nR\tげ\$\t\t\t\tadj-i\ts\t0\t1\t\tい\nR\t気\$\t\t\t\tadj-i\ts\t0\t1\t\tい\nT\t-がる\t-がる\t1. Shows subject’s feelings contrast with what is thought/known about them. 2. Indicates subject's behavior (stands out). Usage: Attach がる to the stem of i-adjectives. It itself conjugates as a godan verb.\nR\tがる\$\t\t\tv5\tadj-i\ts\t0\t2\t\tい\nT\t-やがる\t-やがる\tVulgar auxiliary showing contempt, irritation, or hostility toward the subject. Usage: Attach やがる to